  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">You learn to make effigies that allow you to bring down creatures in the sky, based off of old war techniques employed by the vesperan during and after the War of the Wings. Once per day during your daily preparations, you create an effigy that can cast <em>Earthbind</em> on a flying creature by holding it in your hand and activating it with two actions. The saving throw made is against your spell DC or class DC, whichever is higher. The effigy then crumbles after casting the spell. When you reach 17th level, you can make two effigies per day.</span></p>"
